452: ### Defining animation keyframes
453: 
454: Define the `@keyframes` rules for your `--animate-*` theme variables within `@theme` to include them in your generated CSS:
455: 
456: ```css
457: /* [!code filename:app.css] */
458: @import "tailwindcss";
459: 
460: @theme {
461:   --animate-fade-in-scale: fade-in-scale 0.3s ease-out;
462: 
463:   @keyframes fade-in-scale {
464:     0% {
465:       opacity: 0;
466:       transform: scale(0.95);
467:     }
468:     100% {
469:       opacity: 1;
470:       transform: scale(1);
471:     }
472:   }
473: }
474: ```
475: 
476: If you want your custom `@keyframes` rules to always be included even when not adding an `--animate-*` theme variable, define them outside of `@theme` instead.
477: 
478: ### Referencing other variables
479: 
480: When defining theme variables that reference other variables, use the `inline` option:
481: 
482: ```css
483: /* [!code filename:app.css] */
484: @import "tailwindcss";
485: 
486: /* [!code word:inline] */
487: @theme inline {
488:   --font-sans: var(--font-inter);
489: }
490: ```
491: 
492: Using the `inline` option, the utility class will use the theme variable _value_ instead of referencing the actual theme variable:
493: 
494: ```css
495: /* [!code filename:dist.css] */
496: .font-sans {
497:   font-family: var(--font-inter);
498: }
499: ```
500: 
501: Without using `inline`, your utility classes might resolve to unexpected values because of how variables are resolved in CSS.
502: 
503: For example, this text will fall back to `sans-serif` instead of using `Inter` like you might expect:
504: 
505: ```html
506: <!-- [!code filename:HTML] -->
507: <!-- [!code word:--font-sans\: var(--font-inter, sans-serif);] -->
508: <div id="parent" style="--font-sans: var(--font-inter, sans-serif);">
509:   <!-- [!code word:--font-inter\: Inter; font-family\: var(--font-sans);] -->
510:   <div id="child" style="--font-inter: Inter; font-family: var(--font-sans);">
511:     This text will use the sans-serif font, not Inter.
512:   </div>
513: </div>
514: ```
515: 
516: This happens because `var(--font-sans)` is resolved where `--font-sans` is defined _(on `#parent`)_, and `--font-inter` has no value there since it's not defined until deeper in the tree _(on `#child`)_.
517: 
518: ### Generating all CSS variables
519: 
520: By default only used CSS variables will be generated in the final CSS output. If you want to always generate all CSS variables, you can use the `static` theme option:
521: 
522: ```css
523: /* [!code filename:app.css] */
524: /* [!code word:static] */
525: @import "tailwindcss";
526: 
527: @theme static {
528:   --color-primary: var(--color-red-500);
529:   --color-secondary: var(--color-blue-500);
530: }
531: ```
